id: pm-rust-native-writer-contention
title: Diagnose native writer lock conflicts in cross-platform CI
description: "The existing 50-writer native comment stress test returned lock_conflict on Windows quick shard 1 at 7aa7f9965232ab92e0655e76df607e3ddff2f468. The job was 137153185318 in run 45004486025. The test finished in 14.26 seconds with a configured 60-second acquisition wait. macOS returned the same refusal on fdc1185 and 60456b3, then passed on 7aa7f99. Windows shard 2 passed, as did the merged Linux coverage gate.\n\nThe older issues pm-rust-b6ey and pm-rust-kgfh cover wait-budget exhaustion and diagnostic classification. The current refusal has no verified cause yet."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: ci,concurrency,follow-up
created_at: "2026-11-22T09:07:52.881Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-22T09:07:58.177Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: "Identify whether the refusal originates in acquisition, the 250 ms publication gate wait, or the receipt identity check. Verify admitted writes and their history under equivalent contention on the affected runner."
parent: pm-rust-oracle-1118
files[2]{path,scope}:
  src/mutation.rs,project
  tests/concurrency_contract.rs,project
tests[1]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
